1
00:00:01,550 --> 00:00:04,103
Get us out the door for the library by 08:30.

2
00:00:04,733 --> 00:00:07,460
Getting a household out the door is rarely one task.

3
00:00:07,831 --> 00:00:10,907
Someone carries the plan, the exceptions, and the reminders.

4
00:00:11,655 --> 00:00:13,114
Threshold shares that load.

5
00:00:13,791 --> 00:00:17,873
It remembers that Sam needs a step-free exit and Jo prefers a quiet
cue.

6
00:00:18,449 --> 00:00:21,938
It gives each small job an owner and works out what can happen
together.

7
00:00:22,594 --> 00:00:24,450
A plan is not proof something happened.

8
00:00:25,468 --> 00:00:31,049
People confirm completed tasks. The shared bag becomes available only
when its prerequisites are done.

9
00:00:31,705 --> 00:00:35,289
The lift has stopped working. Find another way that keeps us step-
free.

10
00:00:35,936 --> 00:00:37,386
Now real life changes.

11
00:00:37,884 --> 00:00:46,414
The elevator is out. Threshold moves to the garden ramp, adds the
extra time, and keeps both the accessibility preference and the work
already done.

12
00:00:46,975 --> 00:00:47,869
It is raining now.

13
00:00:48,230 --> 00:00:51,188
Rain adds a dependency the original plan did not have.

14
00:00:51,812 --> 00:00:55,098
The household cannot be marked ready until the new step is confirmed.

15
00:00:55,991 --> 00:00:58,339
Alex can take over Sam’s remaining tasks.

16
00:00:58,717 --> 00:01:02,238
A caregiver can hand over the remaining work without retelling the
morning.

17
00:01:02,857 --> 00:01:06,610
The schedule still respects that one person cannot do two jobs at
once.

18
00:01:07,390 --> 00:01:09,710
Make the hallway glow gently without a sound.

19
00:01:10,335 --> 00:01:12,850
A gentle visual cue appears on the virtual lamp.

20
00:01:13,248 --> 00:01:15,830
It is reversible. Every change leaves a receipt.

21
00:01:16,464 --> 00:01:21,650
Behind this simulated Alexa-plus experience is a real, self-hosted MCP
server.

22
00:01:22,317 --> 00:01:25,441
The official SDK handles Streamable HTTP.

23
00:01:26,133 --> 00:01:32,072
Revisions prevent stale actions, retries do not double-execute, and
context survives a restart.

24
00:01:32,835 --> 00:01:33,417
Threshold.

25
00:01:33,896 --> 00:01:39,210
A little less to carry, and a way forward together.

26
00:01:39,673 --> 00:01:43,592
Alexa+ interaction simulator · real MCP · synthetic household ·
virtual devices.
